      "content": "it just feels like there isn't really a \"safe space\" where the grayness actually goes away. it's just more talking, more pretending, more years of this. it's like i'm just a ghost walking around in a life that belongs to someone else. i look at everything and i just think... wouldn't it be so much more peaceful if it was just quiet? if there was just a way to find that stillness permanently, instead of constantly fighting to stay \"on\" when i'm clearly already gone.",
